From: pmos-lunaa <local>
Subject: [PATCH] tu/kgsl: advertise VK_EXT_physical_device_drm using the display node

LOCAL PATCH for realme-lunaa (SM7325 / Adreno 642L behind KGSL). See the
caveat at the bottom -- not upstreamable as written.

On downstream Qualcomm kernels the Adreno sits behind KGSL (/dev/kgsl-3d0) and
has no DRM node of its own; /dev/dri/renderD128 belongs to the *display*
driver (msm_drm/SDE). Turnip therefore disables VK_EXT_physical_device_drm on
KGSL, having no DRM major/minor to report.

The consequence is that nothing can select the GPU. Every Vulkan consumer that
pairs a Vulkan device with a DRM fd does it through exactly this extension:

  - wlroots 0.20 render/vulkan/vulkan.c:351 matches drmRenderMajor/Minor
    against the DRM fd and logs "VK_EXT_physical_device_drm not supported",
    so WLR_RENDERER=vulkan fails.
  - zink zink_screen.c:1707 does the same match in zink_get_display_device()
    and leaves screen->pdev NULL, so GL-on-Vulkan fails too.

Neither offers an override, and it cascades: with no accelerated compositor
there is no linux-dmabuf advertised to clients, so even plain Vulkan apps
cannot present.

There is exactly one DRM device on such a system, and rendered buffers really
do go to it for scanout, as ION dmabufs which the KGSL backend can already
export (VK_KHR_external_memory_fd is supported). So reporting the display
node's numbers answers the question those consumers are actually asking:
"which DRM device do I share buffers with for this GPU".

Caveat, and why this is not upstreamable as-is: the association is a
convenient fiction -- the GPU is not that DRM device. With more than one DRM
device present this picks an arbitrary one. Upstream would rather teach the
consumers to cope with a GPU that has no DRM node at all.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc	2026-07-29 20:31:27.000000000 +0300
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc	2026-08-26 14:56:43.843945404 +0300
@@ -314,7 +314,11 @@
       .EXT_mutable_descriptor_type = true,
       .EXT_nested_command_buffer = true,
       .EXT_non_seamless_cube_map = true,
-      .EXT_physical_device_drm = !is_kgsl(device->instance),
+      /* On KGSL this is populated from the display DRM node rather than
+       * from a GPU node, so that wlroots and zink can pair the two. The
+       * fields stay zeroed (drmHasRender false) if none is found.
+       */
+      .EXT_physical_device_drm = true,
       .EXT_pipeline_creation_cache_control = true,
       .EXT_pipeline_creation_feedback = true,
 #ifdef TU_USE_WSI_PLATFORM
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc	2026-07-29 20:31:27.000000000 +0300
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc	2026-08-26 15:06:26.582365770 +0300
@@ -5,7 +5,10 @@
 
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
+#include <dirent.h>
 #include <linux/dma-heap.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
+#include <sys/sysmacros.h>
 #include <poll.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <sys/ioctl.h>
@@ -1778,6 +1781,54 @@
    return value;
 }
 
+/* KGSL has no DRM node of its own. Find the DRM device that is present -- on
+ * these downstream Qualcomm kernels that is the display driver (msm_drm/SDE)
+ * -- and report its major/minor as ours, so consumers that pair a Vulkan
+ * device with a DRM fd (wlroots, zink) can select us. See the patch header
+ * for why this association is a deliberate fiction.
+ */
+static void
+tu_kgsl_fill_drm_props(struct tu_physical_device *device)
+{
+   static const char dri_dir[] = "/dev/dri";
+   struct dirent *ent;
+   struct stat st;
+   char buf[64];
+   DIR *dir;
+
+   device->has_master = false;
+   device->has_local = false;
+
+   dir = opendir(dri_dir);
+   if (!dir)
+      return;
+
+   while ((ent = readdir(dir))) {
+      bool render = !strncmp(ent->d_name, "renderD", 7);
+      bool card = !strncmp(ent->d_name, "card", 4);
+
+      if (!render && !card)
+         continue;
+      if (snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "%s/%s", dri_dir, ent->d_name) >=
+          (int) sizeof(buf))
+         continue;
+      if (stat(buf, &st) != 0)
+         continue;
+
+      if (render && !device->has_local) {
+         device->has_local = true;
+         device->local_major = major(st.st_rdev);
+         device->local_minor = minor(st.st_rdev);
+      } else if (card && !device->has_master) {
+         device->has_master = true;
+         device->master_major = major(st.st_rdev);
+         device->master_minor = minor(st.st_rdev);
+      }
+   }
+
+   closedir(dir);
+}
+
 VkResult
 tu_knl_kgsl_load(struct tu_instance *instance, int fd)
 {
@@ -1794,6 +1845,8 @@
       return vk_error(instance, VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY);
    }
 
+   tu_kgsl_fill_drm_props(device);
+
    static const char dma_heap_path[] = "/dev/dma_heap/system";
    static const char ion_path[] = "/dev/ion";
    int dma_fd;
